<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Melian Dialogue</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">416 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Melian Dialogue is a passage in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thucydides">Thucydides</a>' History of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnesian-war">Peloponnesian War</a> recounting negotiations between Athenian envoys and the leaders of Melos in 416 BCE. The Athenians argue that the strong do what they can and the weak suffer what they must, while the Melians appeal to justice and hope. Melos refused to submit and was besieged, its men killed and its women and children enslaved.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/melian-dialogue.jpg" alt="Melian Dialogue" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kurzon · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Melos_Sparta_and_Athens_416_BCE.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
